# Implementation Plan - Architecture Refactor & Standout CV Features

This plan aims to restructure the MediFind codebase to adhere to production-grade software engineering standards. Clean, modular react code and a separated API services layer are the most immediate indicators of a strong developer during placement rounds.

---

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> Review the architectural changes and the suggested resume-boosting features below. We will execute them step-by-step once approved.

### 1. Proposed Standout CV Features (Suggestions to Add)
To make this project stand out to technical interviewers at top product and services companies, we propose adding the following full-stack features:
- **A. Real-Time Socket.io Chat Drawer (Customer ↔ Pharmacy):**
  - Add a live chat tab/widget during active emergency deliveries or reservation pickups.
  - Allows customers to send instant queries (e.g., "Can I collect in 30 minutes?") directly to the pharmacy shop, showing masteries over WebSocket communication.
- **B. Geolocation Route & ETA Drawer:**
  - Enhance the Leaflet map in the split-screen view to render a simple navigation line from the customer coordinate to the selected pharmacy.
  - Compute and print estimated pickup/arrival travel times based on distance.
- **C. CSV Stock Import/Export:**
  - Let pharmacy owners upload a CSV file with columns `Name, Brand, Price, Stock, Category` to batch-populate inventory rather than entering them manually.

